Feature: Writing to and reading from the vehicle
  UPLOAD replaces the mission on the vehicle with the plan. The button shows the number of
  items that it sends. DOWNLOAD reads the mission from the vehicle, so that you can see what
  it flies. EDIT copies the mission from the vehicle into the plan, so that you can change it.

  Expectation: UPLOAD writes the plan to the vehicle
    After the upload, the map goes back to panning. Thus an accidental click does not change
    the plan.
    Given the plan has at least 1 item
    When the operator uploads the plan
    Then the vehicle mission is up to date
    And the map tool is pan

  Expectation: UPLOAD does not send an empty plan
    Given the plan has 0 items
    When the operator uploads the plan
    Then the vehicle mission stays the same

  Expectation: Changing the plan makes the vehicle's copy out of date
    Given the vehicle mission is up to date
    And the map tool is PLAN
    When the operator clicks the map
    Then the vehicle mission is out of date

  Expectation: DOWNLOAD only reads
    When the operator downloads the vehicle's mission
    Then the vehicle mission stays the same
    And the plan stays the same

  Expectation: EDIT brings the vehicle's mission back into the plan
    Given the vehicle mission is out of date
    When the operator edits the vehicle's mission
    Then the vehicle mission is up to date
    And the map tool is PLAN
